1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,380
The manhole is open.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,930
It looks close down there.

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:08,230
"Just a one-minute job," he says.

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,630
But down there...

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,080
there's something you can't see.

6
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:16,850
Hydrogen sulfide.

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,540
Don't trust the smell;

8
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:23,540
at high levels it knocks out your sense of smell, and a few breaths can make you pass out.

9
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:28,980
More than sixty percent of confined-space deaths are would-be rescuers.

10
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:32,060
If your coworker collapses, don't go in after him.

11
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:35,440
Move away and call emergency services, 112.

12
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:45,200
Never enter a confined space without gas testing, ventilation, a supplied-air breathing apparatus and a standby attendant.

